      "id": "holography-koopman",
      "label": "Holography and Koopman: two faces of one inverse problem",
      "description": "Holography generates geometry from entanglement; a general learning machine learns an eigenbasis of its own dynamics. Same inverse problem: recover an operator's eigenstructure from what it does. The HaPPY code is the physical twin of 'forgetting is compression, not deletion'.",
      "url": "https://machengshen.github.io/theory/holography-koopman.md",
      "format": "text/markdown",
      "cognitiveState": "speculative",
      "confidence": 0.5,
      "edges": [{ "relation": "supports", "target": "state-as-closure" }]
    },
    {
      "id": "state-as-closure",
      "label": "State is a closure condition, not a given set",
      "description": "An MDP's state is not handed to you by the world; it is the solution to a closure equation under (world, interface, capacity, telos). Choosing a state is choosing a projection, and choosing a projection is choosing what to forget.",
      "url": "https://machengshen.github.io/theory/state-as-closure.md",
      "format": "text/markdown",
      "cognitiveState": "speculative",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
